{"name":"Bento Box","hex":"#cc363c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bento box","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A partitioned, traditionally lacquered, lunchbox in which a bento (“Japanese takeaway lunch”) is served.","Synonym of bento (“a Japanese takeaway lunch served in a box”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bento_box"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bento","blocks":[{"text":"A bento  is a single-portion take-out or home-packed meal of Japanese origin, often for lunch, typically including rice and packaged in a box with a lid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Bento_box_from_a_grocery_store.jpg/330px-Bento_box_from_a_grocery_store.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bento","wikidata":"Q380532"},{"title":"Box","blocks":[{"text":"A box is a container with rigid sides used for the storage or transportation of its contents. Most boxes have flat, parallel, rectangular sides. Boxes can be very small or very large and can be used for a variety of purposes, from functional to decorative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/L%C3%A5da_-_Livrustkammaren_-_107142.tif/lossy-page1-330px-L%C3%A5da_-_Livrustkammaren_-_107142.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Box","wikidata":"Q188075"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Gotenyama_hiroshige.jpg/500px-Gotenyama_hiroshige.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Gotenyama_hiroshige.jpg/500px-Gotenyama_hiroshige.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hanami bento in the Edo period","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGotenyama_hiroshige.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimed